@flexiarg operator/start-at-the-head-of-the-agreed-list
@title Start At The Head Of The Agreed List
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-4n4PsU turn-7mgeed; first proposed for: A work list has been agreed in the preceding turns (here the M3 items for the Lean-to-Python port) and the session is ready to begin execution.
@why [war-room/wr-13-futonic-debt-is-paid-in-order]

! conclusion: Name the entry point ordinally and begin there; the ordering argument stays settled and the pointer does the work.

  + IF:
    The operator opens with an ordinal pointer — 'Let's start with the first item.'

  + HOWEVER:
    Re-opening the prioritisation at execution time invites drift; but a bare 'start' with no pointer risks the agent beginning on whatever is salient rather than what was agreed first.

  + THEN:
    Name the entry point ordinally and begin there; the ordering argument stays settled and the pointer does the work.

  + BECAUSE:
    WR-13 pays work in dependency order rather than by salience; this proposal is the execution-time instance — the operator enforces the agreed order at the moment work begins by pointing at its head.
